# Copy to /root/.inputrc on the router.
#
# bash built here is not linked against ncurses, so readline cannot read the
# terminfo capabilities kdch1/kich1/kpp/knp and derives no bindings for
# Delete, Insert, PageUp or PageDown -- Delete does nothing at all.  Entware's
# bash is linked against ncurses, which is why it behaves.  Bind them by hand.
# (The real fix is to link bash against the libncursesw.so.6 already shipped
# for htop; this file works meanwhile and costs nothing.)
"\e[3~": delete-char              # Delete
"\e[2~": overwrite-mode           # Insert
"\e[5~": history-search-backward  # PageUp
"\e[6~": history-search-forward   # PageDown
